## 1. Calibration Baseline & the `1 ppQ` ($10^{-15}$) Precision Floor

One **part per quadrillion** (`1 ppQ`) denotes a fractional residual of
$$1\;\mathrm{ppQ} = 10^{-15} = 10^{-6}\;\mathrm{ppb} = 10^{-9}\;\mathrm{ppm} = 10^{-13}\%.$$

Because every dimensional mass prediction $O(m_e, q_0, m_{\pi^\pm})$ scales linearly with $m_e$ or $m_{\pi^\pm}$ and depends smoothly on $q_0$, experimental input uncertainties propagate into every model prediction via the 80-dps Fréchet–Jacobian covariance law $\Sigma_O = J\,\Sigma_\theta\,J^\top$:

| Quantity | Symbol | Value (`80-dps` truncated) | Experimental $1\sigma$ | Relative Floor (`ppb`) | Relative Floor (`ppQ`) | Structural Role |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
{{CALIBRATION_BASELINE_ROWS}}

### Implications for `1 ppQ` Comparisons

1. **Internal mathematical identities (`< 1 ppQ`):** Exact algebraic and numerical round-trip identities (such as the proton mass-identity root inversion at $q_0$, Koide resolvent polynomial identities, and Lanczos/CG eigensolver residuals in few-body $K_A$ plaquettes) hold to `< 10^{-50} ppb` (`< 10^{-44} ppQ`), well beyond `1 ppQ`.
2. **Empirical comparison floor (`830 ppQ` to `1.29e9 ppQ`):** The tightest dimensionless anchor in the framework is $q_0$ itself, whose propagated CODATA uncertainty is `{{Q0_FLOOR_PPQ}} ppQ` (`{{Q0_FLOOR_PPB}} ppb`). Every dimensional mass expressed in MeV inherits at minimum the CODATA electron-mass uncertainty floor of `{{ME_FLOOR_PPQ}} ppQ` (`{{ME_FLOOR_PPB}} ppb`), confirmed across $A = 1\text{--}238$ (`{{NUCLIDE_SIGMA_MIN_PPB}}–{{NUCLIDE_SIGMA_MAX_PPB}} ppb`). Even the most precisely measured non-anchor quantity in physics used here — the fine-structure constant $\alpha_{\mathrm{EM}}^{-1}$ — has a CODATA $1\sigma$ uncertainty of `{{ALPHA_EXP_PPQ}} ppQ` (`{{ALPHA_EXP_PPB}} ppb`).
3. **Bottom-line `1 ppQ` verdict:** **Zero non-anchor observables are empirically testable at or close to `1 ppQ` today.** Current experimental metrology sits $10^5\text{--}10^9\times$ above `1 ppQ` on dimensional observables; in the additive Schwinger Form B arm (where the 1-loop `(1 - h_A^2 α)` factor is proved over $\mathbb{Q}(q)$ by the 4-topology `EmFermionLoop` skein sum), $\alpha_{\mathrm{EM}}^{-1}$ stands at `{{ALPHA_FORMB_ABS_PPQ}} ppQ` (`{{ALPHA_FORMB_REL_PPB}} ppb`, `{{ALPHA_FORMB_PULL}}`$\sigma_{\mathrm{exp}}$), while the conditional two-loop Bloch-$B_3(\mathbb{C})$ Form C evaluation stands at `{{ALPHA_FORMC_ABS_PPQ}} ppQ` (`{{ALPHA_FORMC_REL_PPB}} ppb`, `{{ALPHA_FORMC_PULL}}`$\sigma_{\mathrm{exp}}$).

